{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The sons of the Elohim.</b> The sons of the princes and judges. Another interpretation: the sons of the Elohim — they are the angels who go on missions for the Omnipresent; they too intermingled with them. Every 'elohim' in Scripture is a term of mastery, and this proves it: ״וְאַתָּה תִּהְיֶה לּוֹ לֵאלֹהִים״ (Exodus 4), ״רְאֵה נְתַתִּיךָ אֱלֹהִים״ (ibid. 7)." "<b>For they were good.</b> Rabbi Yudan said: טבת is written (without a vav) — when they would prettify her, adorning her to enter the wedding canopy, a great man would enter and have intercourse with her first (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>From all that they chose.</b> Even a betrothed woman, even a male, and even an animal."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:40.839073408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}